WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:04.155
In Module 1 we built the core Python pattern that
will support the rest of

00:00:04.182 --> 00:00:09.776
the course Variables give values meaningful names
Data types

00:00:09.803 --> 00:00:15.408
tell Python what kind of information it is working
with Arithmetic turns raw values

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:22.072
into derived measures and formatted output helps us
communicate those measures clearly We

00:00:22.098 --> 00:00:27.059
also saw that user input commonly begins as text so
type conversion is an important

00:00:27.072 --> 00:00:33.180
part of preparing data for calculation Most
importantly we practiced reading predicting

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:39.046
running modifying and explaining small pieces of
code In Module

00:00:39.073 --> 00:00:44.733
2 we will add control flow Comparisons if and else
statements for loops and

00:00:44.759 --> 00:00:50.312
while loops will allow our programs to make
decisions and repeat work The small calculations

00:00:50.338 --> 00:00:54.917
from this module will become the building blocks for
more flexible analytical programs
